Content:
I must admit, I am somewhat surprised that Junior Seau* (and I'm sure some others, but definitely him) is not mentioned as a rather large influence/factor/catalyst for the NFL on this.  They were definitely under pressure about it, but then the shocking news of his taking himself from this mortal coil, and how and why he did it... seems to me that this was the final turning point to the whole thing.

He wasn't the only one, no.  But he was probably the most famous and recent player one, loved by nearly all, and the NFL could no longer drag their feet because of it, seems like.  Things started rolling pretty much right after this event, the NFL started to settle and make moves to improve this problem of the game.  They've done better.  I can't say they've done the best possible, there's probably more to do, but certainly I feel Junior's situation shoved everyone into the right gears.

/* - Ow.  
//It's tradition in our house, even to this day, no matter what, and for always.
